This file marks the CertiFlow installation as an *installed* copy.

It is created by the installer and read by settings.py. Because this file is
present, CertiFlow keeps your data in your own user profile:

    %LOCALAPPDATA%\CertiFlow

That folder holds the company profile, the intern database, saved designs and
every generated document. It is deliberately kept out of the program folder so
that:

  * it is always writable, even when the program lives in Program Files;
  * each Windows user gets their own private records;
  * upgrading or uninstalling CertiFlow never touches your data.

The exact path is shown on the About page, with a button to open it.

Deleting this file switches CertiFlow to portable mode, where it looks for data
beside the .exe instead. Only do that for a copy you have moved onto a USB
stick - in an installed copy it will simply hide the records you already have.
